  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Abuja HIV/AIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aimed at providing a comprehensive set of care and support to about 500 people living with HIV and AIDS (PLWHA) in rural communities of Abuja. 

The project will carry out community mobilisation activities to raise awareness on HIV/AIDS, and Tuberculosis. Technical competence of project staff will be enhanced through capacity building in increasing community behavioural change using stepping stones training, voluntary counselling and testing (VCT). Counselling, food supply and material support to PLWHA is a core activity of this project. Other support and care activities includes referral of clients for anti retroviral drugs and treatment of opportunistic infections and home visits by volunteers to those clients who are very ill
Towards the sustainability of the project, an annual 20% reduction in grant and development of sustainability strategy is incorporated in the project.</narrative>
  </description>
